# Line-ending policy.
#
# Git on Windows converts LF to CRLF on checkout by default. That is fine for
# C++ sources, but it silently breaks two things:
#
#   * shell scripts - a CRLF shebang fails on Linux with the memorable and
#     unhelpful "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M"
#   * anything a Linux container reads verbatim
#
# Since CI builds on Linux, Windows and macOS from this one tree, the files
# that must stay LF are pinned here rather than left to each developer's
# core.autocrlf setting.

* text=auto

*.sh       text eol=lf
*.yml      text eol=lf
*.yaml     text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf

*.cpp text
*.h   text
*.txt text
*.md  text
*.cmake text

*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.zst  binary
*.sst  binary
